## Observations

- The dGPU is far ahead of the others. It generates about 6.6x faster than the CPU and about 9.3x faster than the iGPU, and it processes the prompt about 4x faster than the CPU and about 13x faster than the iGPU.
- On this machine the CPU (6 threads) is faster than the iGPU for this model, both for generation and prompt processing.
- Load time is about 2–2.5 s on all three. The dGPU is slightly slower and varies a little more, with runs alternating between about 2.2 s and 2.5 s.
- All three setups are very consistent: run-to-run spread in generation speed is about 1% or less.
- Even with temperature 0 and a fixed seed, the CPU produced **different output** from the two GPU backends. It finished naturally at 387 tokens, while every iGPU and dGPU run hit the 400-token cap. So total time compares fairly between iGPU and dGPU but not against the CPU. Tokens/s is the fairer number to compare across all three.
- The iGPU and dGPU tests used identical flags (`--gpu-layers 999`). The label is the only thing that tells them apart, so the results files are the only record of which GPU each test used.

